  "hints": [
    "<p>Sort the requested floors. If <code>start</code> is itself requested, its request contributes 0 and can be considered already fulfilled.</p>",
    "<p>Once the elevator has visited a leftmost and rightmost floor, every requested floor between them has also been fulfilled. Therefore, use interval DP and keep track of whether the elevator is currently at the left or right endpoint of the visited interval.</p>",
    "<p>When the elevator moves a distance <code>d</code> while <code>k</code> requests are still unfulfilled, the total penalty increases by <code>k * d</code>.</p>",
    "<p>Insert <code>start</code> into the sorted positions and begin with an interval containing only <code>start</code>. From a state <code>[l, r]</code>, expand to the next requested floor on either the left or the right, updating the cost according to the current endpoint and the number of requests still unfulfilled.</p>",
    "<p>There are <code>O(m^2)</code> intervals, where <code>m = requests.length</code>, and two possible endpoint states for each interval. Use 64-bit integers for the penalty.</p>"
